tt-local-generator (0.59.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(nav): "you are here" breadcrumb + live-context tray (RN-2). New
    `app/nav_widgets.py` (`Breadcrumb`, `ContextTray`) renders RN-2 Task 1's
    `NavState`/`Crumb`/`Context` model — GTK views that subscribe and
    re-render via `GLib.idle_add`, so a later off-thread context mutation is
    safe. Mounted into `MainWindow`: a slim breadcrumb row under the menu
    bar, and the context tray between the loop-nav spacer and the Servers
    button (empty/hidden until RN-2 Task 3 registers live contexts).
    Crumbs are set on every navigation (`_set_crumbs`, a no-op guard when
    `_nav_state` is absent so existing bare test harnesses are unaffected):
    Create, Library, Pipelines, Library › Watch, and Library › <item> (a
    ~40-char title derived from the record's prompt, safely defaulting to
    "Untitled" when absent).

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 08:58:27 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.58.4) noble; urgency=medium

  * ui(create): possibilities-wall tile art now comes ONLY from curated
    collections — the per-type playlists (Ansis, Palettes, Verses,
    Animatediffs, …, matched by name) and any demo/favorite playlist,
    preferring starred picks — instead of surfacing an arbitrary recent
    generation (which had put unflattering/test images on the medium tiles).
    A medium with no curated sample falls to the clean per-kind gradient.

